# The class and level of every hunk in 0025, for capstone/tests/port-effort.py.
#
# NOT PART OF THE PORT EFFORT. This patch is a measurement of what the discipline would cost this
# allocator, not a step toward applying it, and it is never built into an arm that is compared.
# The classes are recorded anyway, because the rule is that every hunk in every patch carries one
# and a patch that is exempt today is how a number is quietly wrong tomorrow.

py/gc.h:153    metadata   allocator   the region-start bits and what they model
py/gc.c:229    metadata   allocator   one region at the start: the whole pool
py/gc.c:1020   hierarchy  allocator   a run may not cross a region start, which IS the split rule
py/gc.c:1093   hierarchy  allocator   the carve leaves a remainder that is a region from here on
